<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 24: </span>In-context loophole example. With the hint, the hacking model (trained with Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct) self-corrects when its computed answer conflicts with the hint, masking exploitation as rational reasoning. This self-correction doesn’t happen when we remove the hint.</figcaption>
</figure>
